{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2489","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2489","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2489\",\"parent_revision\":\"24457c57363833919acdee4ac9811da43f3337a68503f4bb495fc3ccf8499060\",\"root_revision\":\"24457c57363833919acdee4ac9811da43f3337a68503f4bb495fc3ccf8499060\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe `SUCCESSFUL_STATUSES` constant \u2014 which defines which task statuses satisfy a dependency check \u2014 is independently defined in three separate modules: `sam_schema/core/dependencies.py`, `backlog_core/operations.py`, and `implementation_manager.py`. These copies are not linked; updating one does not update the others.\\n\\nThis was observed when commit `be6a3aec` added `SKIPPED` to `SUCCESSFUL_STATUSES` to fix issue #2457 (plans deadlocking when a task was skipped). Only the `sam_schema/core/dependencies.py` copy and its direct unit test (`tests_sam/test_dependencies.py`) were updated. The copy relied upon by `tests/test_quality_gate_integration.py` remained stale, encoding the pre-fix behavior. This caused `test_t6_not_ready_after_t5_skipped` to fail on every CI run since that commit, discovered during the 2026-05-29 version-bump refactor session.\\n\\nImpact: any future change to what statuses satisfy a dependency requires updating all three locations. Missing one silently reintroduces failing tests or, worse, incorrect runtime behavior.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: define once and import everywhere to prevent stale copies causing future test failures like test_t6_not_ready_after_t5_skipped\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **successful_statuses constant duplicated across three modules causing silent test failures on update** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: CI failure investigation \u2014 version bump refactor session 2026-05-29\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:1b1dd3feeaaf161db93c84d7d6cec381 -->\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"6710bdecbf52414d140473feb3915f2db7346d18cf30cdf873509dbab787bf81\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCOZpA\"}"}